# {{ component.name }}

A minimal NestJS + TypeScript HTTP backend. `GET /health` returns `{ "status": "ok" }`.
This only checks the scaffold route, not external dependencies or business readiness. Authentication, databases, CORS,
deployment policies and business features are not implemented.

## Code and responsibilities

- `src/main.ts`: composition, listening on `127.0.0.1:3000` and shutdown hooks. Review exposure and ports for real operations.
- `src/app.module.ts`: controller registration; add feature modules when responsibilities have separate reasons to change.
- `src/app.controller.ts`: HTTP response boundary; extract concrete policy/I/O collaborators when needed.
- `tests/health.test.mjs`: starts and closes a real Nest app on an ephemeral loopback port, without an external server.

Do not pre-create a service, interface or repository for every handler. Specify inputs, errors, status codes and resource
ownership, then test actual behavior. Design authorization and DTO validation when those boundaries exist.
This package uses ESM/NodeNext and emitted `.js` paths in relative source imports. `tsc` owns the build to retain Nest
decorator metadata.

## Environment and checks

Use Node 22.22.3 or later and npm 11.11.0. Each component owns its manifest and lock.

```sh
npm install
npm run check
```

Installation creates `package-lock.json`; keep it in Git and use `npm ci` afterward. `check` runs strict typechecking,
TypeScript compilation and the loopback HTTP test, not product, external-integration or deployment acceptance.
`npm start` is a separate loopback-only execution command. Review authentication, input limits and shutdown before
public deployment.

Official metadata/starter pins checked on 2026-10-26: Nest 12.2.0, reflect-metadata 0.2.2, RxJS 7.8.2,
TypeScript 7.0.2 and Node 22 types 22.20.5. Review peer, Node, emit compatibility and the lock together when upgrading.
See [Nest first steps](https://docs.nestjs.com/first-steps) and the
[pinned ESM starter](https://github.com/nestjs/typescript-starter/tree/0b6d71261ba30bb6976949a8653e4a86479a68c1).
CLI, schematics and observability vendor SDKs are not required by this minimal scaffold.

